---
## In short

The ticketing service was down for two hours and ten minutes on 12 March, after a certificate expired on the gateway. No data was lost. The response was quick once the alert reached the on-call team; the alert itself took forty minutes to arrive, and that is what this review proposes to change.

::: metrics
- 2 h 10 | outage | From the first failed request to full service.
- 40 min | before the alert | The longest part of the outage.
- 0 | data lost | Checked against the backups on 13 March.
:::

---
notes: A `---` opens a section. It goes on on the same page, and the engine turns the page when it has to.
---
## What happened

::: timeline
- 09:12 | The certificate expires and requests start to fail.
- 09:52 | The alert reaches the on-call team.
- 10:30 | A new certificate is issued and deployed.
- 11:22 | Full service is confirmed.
:::

The gateway's certificate was renewed by hand once a year, and the reminder went to a mailbox nobody reads since the team moved. The monitoring watched the application behind the gateway, which was healthy, so it stayed silent until customers wrote in.

---
notes: A list of what was decided keeps the words of the source. Whole sentences are read better than fragments on a card.
---
## What we keep

- The on-call team had the right access and needed no one's approval to deploy.
- Customers were told within fifteen minutes of the alert, on the status page and by mail.
- The standard deployment path was followed, with no manual change left behind.

---
notes: Rows of owners and dates are a table. The owners still open are said so, never invented.
---
## What we change

::: table
| Priority | Action | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| High | Renew the gateway's certificate automatically | Infrastructure |
| High | Watch the gateway from outside, as a customer would | To be named |
| Medium | Send every expiry reminder to the team's own channel | Operations |
| Medium | Rehearse this incident once a year | To be named |
:::

> Two owners are still to be named: the committee is asked to decide them on 26 March.
